# Cannon: lobs a shell of light (cannonShell.pre) at the nearest solid demon in its ARC - "Arc (deg)" around its facing
# (the entity's -Z; placed in eighths of a turn, R turns the ghost) - one munition a shot (StructureSystem::tickCannons).
# ONE cell (2x2 m) and 2.2 m tall; the barrel's square mouth reaches ~0.6 m past the cell in front, its top ~1.9 m over
# the stand: on a walkway deck behind a wall, or on the ship's rail, it fires over the wall. It may stand on a road
# piece, a walkway deck or a ship rail tile (it rides that cell's underId). Spawned origin 1.1 over its stand.
# WALK-THROUGH like the Mirror: Layer Cable collides only with Projectile, so players and units pass it
# (StructureSystem::isWalkThrough keeps it out of the nav obstacles and the ship's collider too).
# SHAPE (a placeholder; uniform scales of the baseshapes variants, all boxes): A FIELD GUN - a square bronze barrel (the
# root) raised 15 degrees toward -Z with a wider square mouth and a light glowing in it, on a wooden carriage: two
# cheeks under the barrel, an axle, two big SQUARE wheels (thin plates), and a trail down to the ground behind. The
# CHARGE CRYSTAL over the breech: the munitions are light charges. The child pieces are render-only.
# (The muzzle's place is tickCannons' c_muzzleOut / c_muzzleHeight: keep them in step.)
Prefab gameCannon
